WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.970
Whether you're a believer or a skeptic, you
have to admit that Ghost Adventures is pretty

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.340
darn entertaining. Yet, there's more to this
series than just investigating creepy, abandoned

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.920
areas with extensive paranormal histories.
So let's investigate the untold truths behind

00:00:18.571 --> 00:00:20.651
Zak's spooky collectible

00:00:20.651 --> 00:00:25.041
Whether you love or hate Zak "the Ghost Bro"
Bagans' style, he puts his money where his

00:00:25.041 --> 00:00:30.151
paranormal-loving mouth is, whether cameras
are rolling or not. In August 2015, Bagans

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:35.251
plunked down $32,000 for a van that belonged
to Dr. Jack Kevorkian, who notoriously assisted

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:39.811
with the suicides of 130 confirmed patients.
Bagans says that he doesn't plan on using

00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:43.791
the vehicle for Ghost Adventures, but he does
intend on investigating the van. He told The

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:44.721
New York Daily News:

00:00:44.721 --> 00:00:48.141
"I want to have it to show recognition to
these people and the energy they had at the

00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:51.781
time of their death. I can't wait to get it
and see what I feel off of it…It called

00:00:51.781 --> 00:00:52.811
out to me."

00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:56.041
That's one heck of a collectible, bro.

00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:58.591
The macabre extends to their real lives

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:03.311
Reality can be a lot scarier than any haunted
house. Paranormal investigators Mark and Debbie

00:01:03.311 --> 00:01:07.411
Constantino were featured on Ghost Adventures,
and now may be featured posthumously on a

00:01:07.411 --> 00:01:12.451
true crime series. KRNV-TV reports that the
couple had a long, dark history of domestic

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:17.631
violence. That history came to a tragic head
in September 2015, when Mark killed Debbie,

00:01:17.631 --> 00:01:20.701
as well as himself, after an extensive SWAT
team lockdown.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:23.201
Too scary, even for them

00:01:23.201 --> 00:01:27.901
Bagans purchased a Gary, Indiana home in 2014
after reports that the family living within

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:32.071
it were terrorized by demons. These reports
were backed up by claims from child protective

00:01:32.071 --> 00:01:37.451
services, who also witnessed the creepy activity.
Problem was, the house was actually too scary,

00:01:37.451 --> 00:01:42.861
even for Bagans. TMZ reports that while filming
a documentary in the home, Bagans felt "dark

00:01:42.861 --> 00:01:46.981
energy" and claimed "the demons were the real
deal." Bagans tried exorcising the house but

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:51.441
said his attempts failed. Believing the house
was actually a portal to Hell, Bagans paid

00:01:51.441 --> 00:01:55.591
to have the house demolished in 2016, and
even had the rubble stored in a sealed facility

00:01:55.591 --> 00:02:00.181
so no paranormal energy could escape from
it and affect anyone nearby. Phew.

00:02:00.181 --> 00:02:03.320
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.691
just saw. And leave us a comment to tell us
what Ghost Adventures facts surprised you

00:02:06.691 --> 00:02:07.100
the most...

